# Agent primitives: text agents read as directives, and configuration they
# execute. Named explicitly rather than relying on the `*` wildcard above, so
# these survive any future relaxation of it. `.claude/settings.json` and its
# peers can define hooks that run shell commands, which is why the directories
# matter at least as much as the markdown.
AGENTS.md   @qwts
CLAUDE.md   @qwts
.claude/    @qwts
.codex/     @qwts
.cursor/    @qwts
.mcp.json   @qwts

# Shared skills are reviewed as agent directives and cataloged for cross-repo
# use. Supporting files, when present, are part of that reviewed surface. Skills
# remain in the shared skills home; they are not installed into every harness.
/skills/    @qwts
/skills/author-cli-skill/ @qwts
